HackOS teensy41 size patch to user/hamnix/hamsh.ad (on top of
user/hamnix/hamsh.ad.patch, which the committed file already carries).
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/teensy41/root only.

Reason: a process is one block of the Teensy 4.1's program arena (704 KiB of
on-chip RAM, boards/teensy41/link.ld), and the shell's static arrays are
real memory from its first instruction.  After milestone 3 they were
1,525,832 bytes.  This patch divides by 16 the four arenas the milestone-3
patch divided by 4, at the same sites (array lengths, limits, messages that
quote them, the collector's tables and its headroom thresholds), and shrinks
the separately sized buffers that dominate the rest:

    AST nodes / value cells / list elements   4096 -> 256
    AST kid slots                             8192 -> 512
    interned strings, string GC stage         128 / 64 KiB -> 8 KiB
    tokens per logical input                  4096 -> 256
    collection / sort scratch (COMP_MAX)      4096 -> 256
    variable bindings (SCOPE_MAX)             1024 -> 256
    history ring and history file buffer      48 lines -> 4 (96 KiB -> 8 KiB each)
    glob listing buffer                       64 KiB -> 8 KiB
    user functions                            512 -> 64
    argv slots                                2048 -> 256 (exec takes <= 64 strings)
    script and rc-file buffers                16 KiB -> 8 KiB and 4 KiB

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Measured result (`make BOARD=teensy41`, llvm-size of build/teensy41/user/hamsh.elf):
see REPORT / docs/boards/teensy41.md.  Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/user/hamnix/hamsh.ad --label b/user/hamnix/hamsh.ad user/hamnix/hamsh.ad <copy>

